'''Nimanburru''' is an extinct Western [[Nyulnyulan languages|Nyulnyulan]] language formerly spoken on the eastern shore of the [[Dampier Peninsula]] in the north-west of [[Australia]]. Archival records exist in the [[Australian Institute of Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander Studies]] and some of the material in Hermann Nekes and [[Ernest Ailred Worms]]' ''Australian Languages'' is from the language. 
